## Why This Question Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design robust, low-latency IPC primitives under NUMA-aware multi-producer/multi-consumer contention with precise memory ordering requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Lock-free design, with ABA avoidance via per-slot sequence counters
- NUMA-aware memory placement to minimize cross-socket memory traffic
- Shadow consumer tail optimization to reduce remote cache-line access
- Cache-line alignment to prevent false sharing
- Memory ordering semantics (acquire/release, memory_order_acq_rel)

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
    volatile uint64_t sequence;
    char data[56];
} slot_t;

typedef struct {
    slot_t slots[N] __attribute__((aligned(64)));
    volatile uint64_t head;
    volatile uint64_t tail;
    volatile uint64_t shadow_tail;
} mpmc_queue_t;

static inline int enqueue(mpmc_queue_t* q, const void* data) {
    uint64_t slot = __atomic_fetch_add(&q->tail, 1, __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL);
    slot_t* s = &q->slots[slot & (N - 1)];
    while (s->sequence != slot) { /* spin */ }
    memcpy(s->data, data, 56);
    __atomic_store(&s->sequence, slot + 1, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
    return 0;
}

static inline int dequeue(mpmc_queue_t* q, void* data) {
    uint64_t slot = __atomic_fetch_add(&q->head, 1, __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL);
    slot_t* s = &q->slots[slot & (N - 1)];
    while (s->sequence != slot + 1) { /* spin */ }
    memcpy(data, s->data, 56);
    __atomic_store(&s->sequence, slot + N, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
    return 0;
}
```

## Microbenchmark Outline

To isolate NUMA effects under asymmetric producer/consumer loads:

1. **Setup**: Run producers on socket 0, consumers on socket 1; measure round-trip latency and throughput.
2. **Workload injection**: Vary producer/consumer ratios (e.g., 10:1, 1:10, 5:5) to create asymmetric contention.
3. **Metrics**: Capture remote memory accesses via `numactl --hardware`, cache-miss ratios via `perf stat`, and per-socket latency distributions.
4. **Validation**: Compare interleaved vs. local-only memory placement to quantify NUMA effects; verify shadow tail reduces remote cache-line bouncing.

